  "aciklama": "Amtrak 501 derailed onto Interstate 5 near DuPont. The cause: overspeed on a curve without active positive train control and with an inadequately trained engineer.\n\nFailure chain: First run on new route → Engineer unfamiliar → No active ptc → Curve at 78 mph → Cars fall onto I-5\n\nAnother reconstruction: The Disaster That Ended the Age of the Airship — https://youtu.be/PGOKZhPYo7c\n\nFootage & sources:\n• Archival film: \"NTSB engineers examine Cascades locomotive recorder, December 2017.jpg\" — Wikimedia Commons (public domain / free licence): https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:NTSB_engineers_examine_Cascades_locomotive_recorder%2C_December_2017.jpg\n• Archival film: \"WDTX 1402 (1) postderailment position.jpg\" — Wikimedia Commons (public domain / free licence): https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:WDTX_1402_(1)_postderailment_position.jpg\n• Archival film: \"2017 Cascades derailment aerial view from NTSB preliminary report.jpg\" — Wikimedia Commons (public domain / free licence): https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:2017_Cascades_derailment_aerial_view_from_NTSB_preliminary_report.jpg\n• Archival film: \"Damage to WDTX 1402 (1).jpg\" — Wikimedia Commons (public domain / free licence): https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Damage_to_WDTX_1402_(1).jpg\n\nTechnical references:\n• Wikipedia — 2017 Washington train derailment — https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2017_Washington_train_derailment\n• NTSB — RAR1901 (cited by Wikipedia) — https://www.ntsb.gov/investigations/AccidentReports/Reports/RAR1901.pdf\n\nNarration uses a synthetic voice. Footage is real archival film or licensed stock; anything reconstructed is labelled on screen.\n\nFailure File · Episode 20 · A new engineering failure, reconstructed every day.\n\n#shorts #engineering #Amtrak501 #railways #history",
